#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198057 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "053ab8bb-73ba-54b1-b195-05d4e12c56f1" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Probability of a Union"}] :question/id #uuid "e1b4a2f7-3859-5648-9072-a76486fa1bfa" :question/math-academy-id "e-12933" :question/problem "Given that $P(A)=\\dfrac12$, $P(A \\cap B)=\\dfrac16$, and $P(A \\cup B)=\\dfrac23$, find $P(A'\\cup B')$." :question/worked-solution "First, we calculate $P(B)$ using the addition law:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nP(A∪B) &= P(A) + P(B) - P(A∩B) \\\\\n\\frac{2}{3} &= \\frac{1}{2} + P(B) - \\frac{1}{6} \\\\\nP(B) &= \\frac{2}{3} + \\frac{1}{6} - \\frac{1}{2} \\\\\nP(B) &= \\frac{1}{3}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we construct the corresponding Venn diagram and shade the region $A'\\cup B'$.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/4315/Source/Images/dfa6d853388443970cef0fa6c14c69db.png)\n\nFinally, we have\n\n$$\nP(A'\\cup B') = \\dfrac1{3} + \\dfrac{1}{6} + \\dfrac{1}{3} = \\dfrac56\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198067 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5d5731e2-34fa-5e27-84be-324dc958b509" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Probability of an Intersection"}] :question/id #uuid "252f20b3-8797-5709-96b5-6e9b4aea9677" :question/math-academy-id "e-13034" :question/problem "Given $P(A)=0.3$, $P(B)=0.5$, and $P(A\\cup B)=0.7$, find $P(A'\\cap B)$." :question/worked-solution "First, we calculate $P(A\\cap B)$ using the addition law:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nP(A∪B) &= P(A) + P(B) - P(A∩B) \\\\\n0.7 &= 0.3 + 0.5 - P(A∩B) \\\\\nP(A∩B) &= 0.3 + 0.5 - 0.7 \\\\\nP(A∩B) &= 0.1\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we construct the corresponding Venn diagram and shade the region $A'\\cap B$.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/4315/Source/Images/cb945eebe175b9cf96e1be4d308d32d0.png)\n\nFinally, we have\n\n$$\nP(A'\\cap B) = 0.4\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198068 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "44603ff6-f9c7-5a02-83c1-0e803444bd25" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Probability of a Complement"}] :question/id #uuid "21e52195-d600-5cb5-a8f4-4c9019816694" :question/math-academy-id "e-13035" :question/problem "Given that $P(B)=0.6$, $P(A\\cap B)=0.4$, and $P(A\\cup B)=0.9$, find $P(A')$." :question/worked-solution "First, we calculate $P(A)$ using the addition law:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nP(A∪B) &= P(A) + P(B) - P(A∩B) \\\\\n0.9 &= P(A) + 0.6 - 0.4 \\\\\nP(A) &= 0.9 + 0.4 - 0.6 \\\\\nP(A) &= 0.7\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nP(A^{′}) &= 1 - P(A) \\\\\n&= 1 - 0.7 \\\\\n&= 0.3\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198867 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "053ab8bb-73ba-54b1-b195-05d4e12c56f1" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Probability of a Union"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4c560de1-2886-5b21-af25-6aebde350ba3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5/6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186232871}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4c560de1-2886-5b21-af25-6aebde350ba3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5/6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186232871} :answer-field/id #uuid "ed03e86e-a552-53a0-a7bb-30d435e23e8f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186197447}] :question/id #uuid "212a5751-375f-5d72-9845-bcdb67ca953a" :question/math-academy-id "q-264077" :question/problem "Given that $P(A) = \\frac{1}{4}$, $P(B) = \\frac{1}{6}$, and $P(A∩B) = \\frac{1}{12}$, find $P(A^{′}∪B)$. Do not round your answer.$P(A^{′}∪B) =$\n{{field-1}}"}]}
